{"type":"text","timestamp":1794314461643,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c579e1a2001mXPR76UEZmPUL6","messageID":"msg_1c579d5ca001g8xlss5hmNKRs5","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"text","text":"<think>npm works with a proxy registry. The npm cache is at /tmp/llmlab-deps/npm which is likely read-only. That's fine — npm can install into node_modules.\n\nNote: the Docker build inside the container would use npm's default registry (registry.npmjs.org) — the Dockerfile does `npm ci` which will hit the real registry. The sandbox has \"no other network access\" except public package registries through a read-only cache. Hmm, but the Docker build in this environment... Let me test whether docker is available.\n\nActually, let me check if docker is available in the sandbox.\n\nAlso important: npm ci with package-lock.json in the Docker build requires network. If the grading harness builds the Docker image, it presumably has registry access. I'll just make sure package-lock.json is updated and consistent.\n\nLet's check dockeravailability.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794314461602,"end":1794314461639}}}
