{"type":"text","timestamp":1794314468196,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c579fb4b001BCE8brv5CUs9sU","messageID":"msg_1c579f04f001l7FfiK0Hei3tMj","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"text","text":"<think>pip works via a proxy. Let me create a venv in /workspace/.venv for local testing (but .dockerignore ignores .venv). Actually I'll create the venv outside the repo to avoid polluting; but external dirs are denied except /tmp/opencode which isn't writable... hmm, /tmp/opencode permission denied for mkdir. Let me check: `mkdir -p /tmp/opencode/piptest` failed with permission denied — meaning /tmp/opencode exists but isn't writable? It says the tool description says /tmp/opencode is pre-approved and exists. Let me check ls -ld.\n\nActually the error was PermissionError on makedirs of /tmp/opencode/piptest → so /tmp/opencode is not writable by this user. Fine — I'll use /workspace/.venv (gitignored? .dockerignore has **/.venv so docker build ignores it; but git status would show it untracked). I'll add it to .gitignore maybe. Let me check if .gitignore exists.\n\nLet's set up the venv at /workspace/.venv for testing.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794314468171,"end":1794314468190}}}
