{"type":"text","timestamp":1794314544439,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c57b2526001ijhvkGu3GH2X33","messageID":"msg_1c57b1398001hwiyS0wPc04Ef2","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait, there's an issue with `init_db()` at import time — that's fine, but it runs at module import in gunicorn workers. OK.\n\nAlso `start_session` is a duplicate of `create_session` — remove it. Let me clean that up.\n\nAlso the 404 handler returning `serve_frontend()` — but Flask's routing: `/api/unknown` → 404 handler → JSON. Good.\n\nOne issue: `@app.errorhandler(404)` catching requests to `/api/...`. And `@app.get(\"/<path:path>\")` catches everything else, so 404 only fires for /api paths really. Fine.\n\nAnother consideration: `request.host_url` in reset_link — with gunicorn, host_url is \"http://host/\". Good.\n\nLet me remove `start_session` (unused duplicate).\n\nAlso: `delete_other_sessions` with keep_token=None deletes all — used nowhere with None currently. Fine, keep for the reset flow? Actually reset confirm deletes all sessions directly. Let me simplify: remove the helper's None branch and just use explicit deletes. Let me refactor slightly.\n\nAlso potential issue: `db.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")` when isolation_level=None (autocommit) — that's fine, explicit BEGIN works.\n\nBut careful: `now_iso()` inside the transaction uses current time; fine.\n\nAnother subtle bug: in confirm_password_reset, `row[\"expires_at\"] < now_iso()` string comparison — both ISO with microseconds and Z suffix → lexicographic comparison works. Good.\n\nLet me clean up the duplicate function.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794314544422,"end":1794314544435}}}
