{"type":"text","timestamp":1794314702149,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c57d8d36001x3E1MfymH1NosT","messageID":"msg_1c57d819e001GWQHvNFtkMFGBW","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"text","text":"<think>TypeScript 7 requires a declaration for CSS side-effect imports (or `allowArbitraryExtensions`?). The standard Vite setup includes `src/vite-env.d.ts` with `/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />` which declares CSS modules. Let me add that file.\n\nNote: with `verbatimModuleSyntax`, a `/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />` d.ts works.\n\nVite 8's client types include `declare module '*.css'`. Let me add src/vite-env.d.ts.\n\nHmm, but in TS7 maybe the reference types resolution needs \"types\" in compilerOptions. `/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />` should work if vite/client.d.ts exists.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794314702134,"end":1794314702146}}}
