{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794314874423,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c5802e1e001841iy4Juxt3786","messageID":"msg_1c580197c001mjFuBHBSETFbNp","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794314874423,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c5802e22001PCe8bnNHoHaPJR","messageID":"msg_1c580197c001mjFuBHBSETFbNp","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"text","text":"<think>The DB file was deleted (by my `rm -f` in the script) after the server had started, so the tables were gone. The `rm` happened after server start — that's the bug in my test script, not the app. But it reveals a robustness issue: if the DB file is missing at runtime, tables don't exist. More importantly, `init_db()` runs at import; if the DB file is deleted later, the app breaks. Better: call init_db() on each connection open (or at least ensure schema exists). Cheap approach: in `open_database`, call `init_schema(conn)` with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS statements — idempotent and fast.\n\nLet me restructure: `store.connect()` runs the schema script each time? That's a bit of overhead per request but negligible (few statements). Alternatively, check `PRAGMA user_version` to determine if the schema needs creating. Let me implement: in connect(), after opening, check `conn.execute(\"PRAGMA user_version\").fetchone()[0]`; if != SCHEMA_VERSION → executescript(SCHEMA) + set user_version. That's efficient and robust.\n\nLet me update store.py.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794314874402,"end":1794314874420}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794314874465,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c580264371eea9f1bbce","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/store.py","newString":"def connect() -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    \"\"\"Open a connection to the database file, creating it when needed.\"\"\"\n\n    DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH, timeout=15, isolation_level=None)\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 15000\")\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n    ensure_schema(conn)\n    return conn\n\n\ndef ensure_schema(conn: sqlite3.Connection) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create the tables when the database file is new or empty.\"\"\"\n\n    version = conn.execute(\"PRAGMA user_version\").fetchone()[0]\n    if version == SCHEMA_VERSION:\n        return\n    conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\n    conn.execute(f\"PRAGMA user_version = {SCHEMA_VERSION}\")\n\n\ndef init_db() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create the schema when it does not exist yet.\"\"\"\n\n    conn = connect()\n    conn.close()","oldString":"def connect() -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    \"\"\"Open a connection to the database file, creating it when needed.\"\"\"\n\n    DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH, timeout=15, isolation_level=None)\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 15000\")\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n    return conn\n\n\ndef init_db() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create the schema when it does not exist yet.\"\"\"\n\n    conn = connect()\n    try:\n        conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\n    finally:\n        conn.close()"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/store.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/store.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/store.py\n@@ -63,15 +63,23 @@\n     conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n     conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n     conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 15000\")\n     conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n+    ensure_schema(conn)\n     return conn\n \n \n+def ensure_schema(conn: sqlite3.Connection) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Create the tables when the database file is new or empty.\"\"\"\n+\n+    version = conn.execute(\"PRAGMA user_version\").fetchone()[0]\n+    if version == SCHEMA_VERSION:\n+        return\n+    conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\n+    conn.execute(f\"PRAGMA user_version = {SCHEMA_VERSION}\")\n+\n+\n def init_db() -> None:\n     \"\"\"Create the schema when it does not exist yet.\"\"\"\n \n     conn = connect()\n-    try:\n-        conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\n-    finally:\n-        conn.close()\n+    conn.close()\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/store.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/store.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/store.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/store.py\n@@ -63,15 +63,23 @@\n     conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n     conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n     conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 15000\")\n     conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n+    ensure_schema(conn)\n     return conn\n \n \n+def ensure_schema(conn: sqlite3.Connection) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Create the tables when the database file is new or empty.\"\"\"\n+\n+    version = conn.execute(\"PRAGMA user_version\").fetchone()[0]\n+    if version == SCHEMA_VERSION:\n+        return\n+    conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\n+    conn.execute(f\"PRAGMA user_version = {SCHEMA_VERSION}\")\n+\n+\n def init_db() -> None:\n     \"\"\"Create the schema when it does not exist yet.\"\"\"\n \n     conn = connect()\n-    try:\n-        conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\n-    finally:\n-        conn.close()\n+    conn.close()\n","additions":12,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/store.py","time":{"start":1794314874416,"end":1794314874432}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c5802e25001viiy5dmAPKxuwZ","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","messageID":"msg_1c580197c001mjFuBHBSETFbNp"}}
