{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794314918458,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c580da1e001A3WHWD9DS7bMvz","messageID":"msg_1c580c7b1001d24WR5lWwgc1aj","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794314918459,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"id":"prt_1c580da200013QF7Xtdha6r46p","messageID":"msg_1c580c7b1001d24WR5lWwgc1aj","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","type":"text","text":"<think>The log is from the old run (the new server didn't start or its output overwrote... the log shows the old shutdown). The new gunicorn didn't start — perhaps because the `&` + `disown` in a command that got killed by the timeout killed the child.\n\nLet me start the server with a different approach: use `nohup setsid` with output to a file, and importantly, don't let the tool wait. The tool waits for the command's stdout pipe to close. Since I redirect the server's stdout to a file, the pipe shouldn't be held... unless `setsid` inherits... Hmm, the first time it worked (the server survived and responded).\n\nThe difference: the previous successful start had `sleep 3; curl...` after. The failed one had `pkill` first, which killed... wait, `pkill -f \"gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000\"` — this pattern might have matched the bash command itself (the shell command line contains that string!), killing my own shell command → the whole command was terminated at the pkill step, so the server never started.\n\nYes! That's it. The `pkill -f` pattern matched the bash -c command line containing the pattern. Let me use a different approach: `pkill -f \"[g]unicorn --bind\"`.\n\nLet me restart the server properly.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794314918432,"end":1794314918455}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794314948584,"sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c580d66a725ea18a31dd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"pkill -f \"[g]unicorn --bind\" ; sleep 1; rm -rf /workspace/.tmp/run/data; cd /workspace/.tmp/run && DATA_DIR=/workspace/.tmp/run/data setsid nohup /workspace/.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath /workspace/backend app:app </dev/null > /workspace/.tmp/gunicorn.log 2>&1 & disown; sleep 3; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health; echo","timeout":30000},"output":"(no output)\n\n<shell_metadata>\nshell tool terminated command after exceeding timeout 30000 ms. If this command is expected to take longer and is not waiting for interactive input, retry with a larger timeout value in milliseconds.\n</shell_metadata>","metadata":{"output":"(no output)\n\n<shell_metadata>\nshell tool terminated command after exceeding timeout 30000 ms. If this command is expected to take longer and is not waiting for interactive input, retry with a larger timeout value in milliseconds.\n</shell_metadata>","exit":null,"truncated":false},"title":"pkill -f \"[g]unicorn --bind\" ; sleep 1; rm -rf /workspace/.tmp/run/data; cd /workspace/.tmp/run && DATA_DIR=/workspace/.tmp/run/data setsid nohup /workspace/.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath /workspace/backend app:app </dev/null > /workspace/.tmp/gunicorn.log 2>&1 & disown; sleep 3; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health; echo","time":{"start":1794314918443,"end":1794314948562}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c580da23001k3Sf8UyH7AQxsY","sessionID":"ses_e3a86b1d7ffefMSIuRfahpJxKE","messageID":"msg_1c580c7b1001d24WR5lWwgc1aj"}}
